# TCGA-BRCA Gene Expression Analysis

## Project Overview

This project explores RNA-seq gene expression patterns in breast cancer using data from The Cancer Genome Atlas Breast Invasive Carcinoma (TCGA-BRCA) project. The analysis focuses on two genes, ESR1 and PGR, which are involved in hormone receptor signaling.

## Analysis

Using R, the project examines gene expression across 1,231 TCGA-BRCA samples through descriptive statistics and five visualizations:

- Histogram of ESR1 expression
- Scatter plot of ESR1 and PGR expression
- Box plot of ESR1 expression across PAM50 subtypes
- Heatmap of the 10 genes with the highest average raw counts
- Density plot of ESR1 expression across PAM50 subtypes

## Tools

- R and RStudio
- tidyverse and ggplot2
- ComplexHeatmap
- circlize
- R Markdown
- LaTeX

## Data

The analysis uses TCGA-BRCA RNA-seq count data and associated sample metadata. The original data are available through the National Cancer Institute's Genomic Data Commons: https://portal.gdc.cancer.gov/

The R Markdown analysis expects the count matrix and metadata files in a `data/` directory.

## Project Files

- `GulzarArwa-FinalProject.Rmd` — R code and analysis
- LaTeX source (`.tex`) — Scientific report
- PNG figures — Five gene expression visualizations

## Limitations

The analysis uses raw, unnormalized RNA-seq counts and is intended for descriptive exploration rather than statistical inference.
